$DIR/main.p:47:2: cannot pass f to viaHelper, which keeps it after returning
    f is a function literal that uses n. A function literal that uses variables
    of the function around it refers to those variables where they live, in
    helper's frame (n is declared at main.p:44). viaHelper passes f to start
    (main.p:27), which passes f to a task statement (main.p:23), so f would
    outlive n.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Change viaHelper to take a value or an owner, which it can keep: an owned[T]
    from new, a shared[T], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)

